"Smart+ Upgraded Experience | TikTok for Business (https://ads.tiktok.com/resources/help/article/about-updates-to-smart-plus?lang=en-GB)\nciteturn564view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ads.tiktok.com/resources/help/article/about-updates-to-smart-plus?lang=en-GB\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 83\nL0: 【0†Business Resource Centre】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Business Help Centre】 【2†Partner enablement】 【3†What's new】\nL3: # About upgrades to Smart+\nL4: \nL5: Last updated: October 2026\nL6: \nL7: Note: this feature may not be available to you yet. Contact your TikTok account manager or contact customer support for more information.\nL8: Smart+ is evolving to deliver features you expect, controls you want, and performance you need across every lower-funnel objective. Manual and Smart+ experiences have been unified into a single flow, offering a more flexible ad buying experience where you can fine-tune your campaigns with new levels of control. With the upgraded experience, you can tailor your campaign to full automation, partial automation, or fully manual.\nL9: ## What's new\nL10: \nL11: Campaign creation  | One unified campaign creation flow for a simpler, more streamlined setup\nL12: Targeting & placement  | More targeting options with the ability to enforce settings\nL13: Creative  | Creative combination control & reporting, multi-URL capabilities, and up to 50 asset groups\nL14: Campaign structure  | Flexible campaign structure with multiple ad groups\nL15: Budget  | More flexibility with budget distribution\nL16: ## Availability\nL17: \nL18: The upgraded Smart+ experience is available for the Traffic, Sales, Lead Generation and App Promotion objectives.\nL19: \nL20: ## Navigating the updated flow\nL21: ### Campaign level\nL22: \nL23: When you create a new Smart+ campaign, you'll first need to decide your budget strategy:\nL24: \nL25:   * Automatic campaign budget: Enter one budget for your entire campaign, and we'll automatically allocate it across ad group for optimal performance.\nL26: \nL27:   * Custom ad group budgets: Input different budgets and optimization settings for each ad group.\nL28: \nL29: Learn more about 【4†budget strategy for the upgraded Smart+ experience】.\nL30: Smart+ campaigns now have automated rules. Note: When using an automatic campaign budget strategy, bid adjustments will apply to all ad groups. Additionally, if you run an automatic budget campaign, all ad groups must use the same budget and bid strategies.\nL31: ### Ad group level\nL32: \nL33: At the ad group level, you can edit the following settings:\nL34: \nL35:   * Optimization and bidding: includes your desired optimization location, the optimization goal, and the Target CPA.\nL36: \nL37:   * Budget and schedule: available budget settings will depend on whether you are using the automatic campaign budget strategy.\nL38:   * Audience targeting: choose the appropriate targeting strategy, including whether to use audience controls or switch to manual targeting. Learn more about 【5†targeting in the upgraded Smart+ experience】.\nL39: \nL40:   * Placements and brand safety: 【6†Automatic placement】 is set by default. If you prefer more manual control, choose the Select placement option and choose the specific placements you'd like to include. You can additionally choose brand safety options.\nL41: ### Ad level\nL42: \nL43: At the ad level, you'll add your creative assets from your TikTok posts or creative library. If you include a destination URL, a Recommended tab will appear in the Add creative window, suggesting assets based on your website content and recent performance data. Ads will be generated based on combinations of your videos and ad texts, and the high-performing combinations will be automatically delivered.\nL44: You can 【7†add multiple ads】, and each ad functions like an asset group, with its own destination URL, product set, and up to 50 creative assets. This new structure enables you to include multiple URLs and product sets within the same ad group or campaign.\nL45: ### Reporting updates\nL46: \nL47: Upgraded Smart+ introduces creative-level reporting within the ad list. You can now view performance data grouped by creative material ID (video, image, catalog, text) to better identify top-performing combinations.\nL48: \nL49: Additional automation features available at the ad level include:\nL50:   * Enhanced ad formats: New ad formats such as CTA creation have been introduced to help you maximize campaign impact. The system now automatically generates tailored ad formats with pre-filled details based on your inputs, such as product information. Learn more 【8†about product information and ad format variations】.\nL51:   * Simplified Spark Ads setup: Spark Ads selection and creation has been simplified to deliver a more efficient setup experience and help you fully unlock the value of your organic content. Learn more about 【9†creating Spark Ads for Smart+ campaigns】.\nL52:   * New Smart+ Symphony tools: Introducing 【10†Recommended Creatives】 and 【11†Automatic Enhancements】, two Gen AI powered tools designed to streamline campaign creatives. Recommended Creatives can generate new assets, while Automatic Enhancements optimizes your assets with resizing, quality boosts, translation and dubbing, and more.\nL53:   * Flexible Catalog Ads creation: 【12†Catalog Ads】 can now be implemented at the ad level, providing greater flexibility in how advertisers can adopt catalog creatives and allowing both catalog and non-catalog ads to run within the same campaign.\nL54: \nL55: Tip: You can download our upgraded Smart+ experience guide to learn more about automation features at the ad level:\nL56: \nL57: 【13†Image†lf-tt4b.tiktokcdn.com】\nL58: \nL59: Upgraded Smart+ Experience - 4 pager .pdf (2.99 MB)\nL60: ## Next steps\nL61: \nL62: Learn 【14†how to create a campaign in the upgraded Smart+ experience】.\nL63: \nL64: 【15†Image†sf16-website-login.neutral.ttwstatic.com】\nL65: \nL66: Log in for a personalised experience\nL67: \nL68: 【16†Sign up】\nL69: \nL70: Resources\nL71: \nL72: * 【17†TikTok Shop Academy†seller-us.tiktok.com】\nL73: * 【18†TikTok Help Center†support.tiktok.com】\nL74: * 【19†TikTok Academy†www.tiktokacademy.com】\nL75: * 【20†TikTok for Business】\nL76: * 【21†Creative Center】\nL77: * 【22†Agentic Hub】\nL78: \nL79: * 【23†Terms and Policies】\nL80: * 【24†Privacy†www.tiktok.com】\nL81: \nL82: ©2026 TikTok For Business\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAnnouncement from the new TikTok USDS Joint Venture LLC - Newsroom | TikTok (https://newsroom.tiktok.com/announcement-from-the-new-tiktok-usds-joint-venture-llc?lang=en)\nciteturn564view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://newsroom.tiktok.com/announcement-from-the-new-tiktok-usds-joint-venture-llc?lang=en\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 76\nL0: 【0†About†www.tiktok.com】【1†Newsroom】【2†Careers†lifeattiktok.com】【3†Contact†www.tiktok.com】\nL1: \nL2: 【4†Watch TikTok†www.tiktok.com】\nL3: \nL4: January 23, 2026•【5†Company】, 【6†News】\nL5: # Announcement from the new TikTok USDS Joint Venture LLC\nL6: \nL7: Below is today’s official announcement made by 【7†TikTok USDS Joint Venture LLC†usdsjv.tiktok.com】.\nL8: \nL9: __\nL10: \nL11: TikTok USDS Joint Venture LLC Established in Compliance with U.S. Regulatory Requirements\nL12: Today, TikTok USDS Joint Venture LLC has been established in compliance with the Executive Order signed by President Trump on September 25, 2025, now enabling more than 200 million Americans and 7.5 million businesses to continue to discover, create, and thrive as part of TikTok's vibrant global community and experience.\nL13: The majority American owned Joint Venture will operate under defined safeguards that protect national security through comprehensive data protections, algorithm security, content moderation, and software assurances for U.S. users.\nL14: TikTok USDS Joint Venture's mandate is to secure U.S. user data, apps and the algorithm through comprehensive data privacy and cybersecurity measures. It will safeguard the U.S. content ecosystem through robust trust and safety policies and content moderation while ensuring continuous accountability through transparency reporting and third-party certifications.\nL15:   * Data Protection: U.S. user data will be protected by USDS Joint Venture in Oracle's secure U.S. cloud environment. The Joint Venture will operate a comprehensive data privacy and cybersecurity program that is audited and certified by third party cybersecurity experts.\nL16: The program will adhere to major industry standards, including the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) CSF and 800-53 and ISO 27001 as well as the Cybersecurity & Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) Security Requirements for Restricted Transactions.\nL17:   * Algorithm Security: The Joint Venture will retrain, test, and update the content recommendation algorithm on U.S. user data. The content recommendation algorithm will be secured in Oracle's U.S. cloud environment.\nL18:   * Software Assurance: The Joint Venture will secure U.S. apps through software assurance protocols, and review and validate source code on an ongoing basis, assisted by its Trusted Security Partner, Oracle.\nL19:   * Trust & Safety: The Joint Venture will safeguard the U.S. content ecosystem and have decision-making authority for trust and safety policies and content moderation.\nL20: Interoperability enables the Joint Venture to provide U.S. users with a global TikTok experience, ensuring U.S. creators can be discovered and businesses can operate on a global scale. TikTok global's U.S. entities will manage global product interoperability and certain commercial activities, including e-commerce, advertising, and marketing.\nL21: The Joint Venture, built on the foundation of the TikTok U.S. Data Security (USDS) organization, will operate as an independent entity governed by the following seven-member, majority-American board of directors:\nL22:   * Shou Chew – Director: Shou Chew is the Chief Executive Officer of TikTok, where he leads the company's global businesses and strategy.\nL23:   * Timothy Dattels – Director: Timothy Dattels is a Senior Advisor to TPG Global, where he previously served as a Partner, Chairman of TPG Asia, and a member of the firm’s Executive Committee.\nL24:   * Mark Dooley – Director: Mark Dooley is a Managing Director at Susquehanna International Group, which he joined in 1987 as one of the firm’s original employees. He serves on the firm’s Management Committee, overseeing its global trading operations.\nL25:   * Egon Durban – Director: Egon Durban is Co-CEO of Silver Lake, which he joined in 1999 as a founding principal. He serves on multiple boards across Silver Lake’s portfolio including Dell Technologies, Qualtrics, TKO Group, Unity, and Waymo.\nL26:   * Raul Fernandez – Independent Director and Chair of the Security Committee: Raul Fernandez is President and Chief Executive Officer of DXC Technology and a member of its Board of Directors. He brings more than three decades of experience at the intersection of technology, risk, and national security.\nL27:   * Kenneth Glueck – Director: Kenneth Glueck is Executive Vice President in the Office of the Chief Executive Officer at Oracle, where he advises the CEO on global strategy, business, M&A, technology, policy, and regulatory matters, and leads Global Corporate Affairs and Global Corporate Communications.\nL28:   * David Scott – Director and Security Committee: David Scott is Chief Strategy and Safety Officer at MGX, where he works closely with the fund’s leadership to set MGX’s strategic direction, including overseeing the governance of security and safety risks associated with emerging AI technologies.\nL29: The Joint Venture will be led by Adam Presser, who was appointed today as CEO by the Board as one of its first actions. He will be joined by Will Farrell as Chief Security Officer.\nL30:   * Adam Presser – Chief Executive Officer: Adam Presser serves as CEO of TikTok USDS Joint Venture. Under his leadership, the Joint Venture will secure U.S. user data, apps, and the algorithm, while driving business growth for TikTok, CapCut, and additional apps and websites in the U.S. Previously, Adam held roles at TikTok USDS, TikTok, and WarnerMedia.\nL31:   * Will Farrell – Chief Security Officer: Will Farrell serves as Chief Security Officer of TikTok USDS Joint Venture, where he oversees the Joint Venture's comprehensive data privacy and cybersecurity program. Previously, Will held roles at TikTok USDS, TikTok, and Booz Allen Hamilton.\nL32: TikTok USDS Joint Venture has three managing investors, Silver Lake, Oracle and MGX, each holding 15%.\nL33: Completing the full consortium of investors are: Dell Family Office, the investment firm of Michael Dell, Founder, Chairman and CEO of Dell Technologies; Vastmere Strategic Investments, LLC, an affiliate of Susquehanna International Group, LLP; Alpha Wave Partners; Revolution; Merritt Way, LLC controlled and managed by partners of Dragoneer; Via Nova, an affiliate of General Atlantic; Virgo LI, Inc., investment arm of a foundation established by Yuri and Julia Milner in support of science; and NJJ Capital, the family office of Xavier Niel, a French entrepreneur and pioneer in telecommunications.\nL34: ByteDance retains 19.9% of the Joint Venture.\nL35: The safeguards provided by the Joint Venture will also cover CapCut, and Lemon8, and a portfolio of other apps and websites in the U.S.\nL36: \nL37: About TikTok USDS Joint Venture LLC\nL38: TikTok USDS Joint Venture LLC is dedicated to the safety and security of millions of Americans who create, discover, and connect with what they love on the apps we operate. The Joint Venture has been established in compliance with the Executive Order signed by President Trump on September 25, 2025. Our foundation is a comprehensive data privacy and cybersecurity program we operate under defined safeguards to protect national security and secure U.S. user data, apps and the algorithm. We safeguard the U.S.\nL39: content ecosystem, holding decision-making authority for trust and safety policies and moderation. USDS Joint Venture helps ensure Americans can continue to express their creativity, discover new hobbies and interests, and build thriving communities and businesses on a global scale.\nL40:   * Language\nL41:     * English (US)\nL42: \nL43:   * Company\nL44:     * 【0†About†www.tiktok.com】\nL45:     * 【1†Newsroom】\nL46:     * 【8†Store†shop.tiktok.com】\nL47:     * 【3†Contact†www.tiktok.com】\nL48:     * 【2†Careers†lifeattiktok.com】\nL49:     * 【9†ByteDance†www.bytedance.com】\nL50:   * Programs\nL51:     * 【10†TikTok For Good†www.tiktok.com】\nL52:     * 【11†TikTok For Developers†developers.tiktok.com】\nL53:     * 【12†Effect House†effecthouse.tiktok.com】\nL54:     * 【13†Advertise†ads.tiktok.com】\nL55:     * 【14†Browse†www.tiktok.com】\nL56:     * 【15†Embed†www.tiktok.com】\nL57:     * 【16†Rewards†www.tiktok.com】\nL58:     * 【0†Scaled LIVE Rewards†www.tiktok.com】\nL59:   * Resources\nL60:     * 【17†Help Center†support.tiktok.com】\nL61:     * 【18†Safety Center†www.tiktok.com】\nL62:     * 【19†Privacy Center†www.tiktok.com】\nL63:     * 【20†Creator Academy†www.tiktok.com】\nL64:     * 【21†Community Guidelines†www.tiktok.com】\nL65:     * 【22†Transparency†www.tiktok.com】\nL66:     * 【23†Accessibility†www.tiktok.com】\nL67: \nL68:   * Social\nL69:     * 【4†TikTok†www.tiktok.com】\nL70:     * 【24†LinkedIn†www.linkedin.com】\nL71:     * 【25†Youtube†www.youtube.com】\nL72:     * 【26†Instagram†www.instagram.com】\nL73: 【27†Terms of Service†www.tiktok.com】【28†Privacy†www.tiktok.com】【29†Intellectual Property Policy†www.tiktok.com】【30†Law Enforcement†www.tiktok.com】\nL74: \nL75: © 2025 TikTok\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUse Cookies with TikTok Pixel | TikTok For Business (https://ads.tiktok.com/resources/help/article/using-cookies-with-tiktok-pixel)\nciteturn564view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ads.tiktok.com/resources/help/article/using-cookies-with-tiktok-pixel\",\"lineno\":9}); Total lines: 67\nL0: 【0†Business Resource Centre】\nL1: \nL2: 【0†Business Help Centre】 【1†Partner enablement】 【2†What's new】\nL3: \nL4: # About using cookies with TikTok Pixel\nL5: \nL6: Last updated: July 2025\nL7: \nL8: Cookies are small text files that help match events with people who engage with your content on TikTok and can be used to enhance measurement accuracy and ad campaign optimization. These cookies can also assist in building retargeting and engagement audiences, depending on your settings and those of your visitors.\nL9: ## Availability\nL10: \nL11:   * Partners eligible for first- and third-party cookies: WooCommerce, Wordpress, BigCommerce, VTex, Cafe24, Shopify, OpenCart, Ecwid, TRAY, Loja Integrada, Kyte, Mercado Shops, Nuvemshop, Base, Haravan, Shopline, FutureShop, Shoplazza, Anytrack, Apptrian, Blotout, Commanders Act, Elevar, Google Tag Manager, Grivy, Journify, Segment, SignalSight (ZZG), Tealium, Ticketmaster, Rudderstack\nL12: \nL13:   * Cookies expire after 13 months from being set onto a browser, or last used.\nL14:   * You can use third-party cookies with Events API as an external_id parameter. You can pass first-party cookies through a dual pixel and Events API setup to enable better matching.\nL15: ## Benefits\nL16: \nL17:   * Measure More Conversions: Connect ads seen on TikTok to conversion events on your website, app, or store, to help you better understand ROI and the impact of your TikTok ads.\nL18: \nL19:   * Improve Ad Delivery and Decrease CPAs: Identify and deliver ads to people who are more likely to take the desired action, increasing efficiency and reducing costs.\nL20: \nL21:   * Expand Your Reach: Match your website visitors with people on TikTok, to expand audience sizes for solutions like web retargeting.\nL22:   * Enhanced Matching Capabilities: Advanced Matching, combined with first- and third-party cookies, ensures the best possible matching, especially as third-party cookies face deprecation.\nL23: \nL24:   * No Change in Conversion Windows: Allowing cookies will not alter your pixel conversion windows. Cookies enhance the matching and attribution process, acting as a supplement to Advanced Matching.\nL25: ## Key concepts\nL26: \nL27:   * First-Party Cookies: These cookies are created and owned by your website and are used to recognize a person on your domain only. They are enabled by default with the TikTok Pixel but can be disabled in your pixel settings. First-party cookies are essential for maintaining user privacy and ensuring that your website can recognize returning visitors.\nL28:   * Third-Party Cookies: Created and owned by TikTok via TikTok's server, third-party cookies extend beyond individual domains. They are used to recognize and match events across different websites and are enabled by default with the TikTok Pixel.\nL29:   * TikTok Pangle Cookies: These cookies are specific to regions supported by TikTok Pangle and are read rather than set by the TikTok Pixel. In jurisdictions where advertisers use the TikTok Pangle Ad Network, the TikTok Pixel may collect TikTok Pangle cookies to measure ad campaigns.\nL30: ## Key considerations\nL31: \nL32:   * Turning Off First-Party Cookies: If you decide to turn off first-party cookie usage after initially having it on, no new first-party cookies will be set moving forward. Existing first-party cookies will continue to operate until they expire over time.\nL33:   * Lack of Developer Resources: If you don't have developer resources to update your website, consider integrating third-party consent management platforms to manage cookie consent. These platforms often provide technical resources and implementation options, including banner design and more, to help you manage cookie usage effectively. This can ensure that your TikTok Pixel is used in compliance with user consent.\nL34: \nL35: 【3†Image: Use only third-party cookies with the TikTok Pixel GIF†lf-tt4b.tiktokcdn.com】\nL36: ## TikTok cookies specifications\nL37: Cookie name  | _ttp  | _ttp  | ttcsid_, ttcsid_<pixel code>  | ttclid  | _pangle\nL38: Cookie domain  | Your website domain  | .tiktok.com  | Your website domain  | Your website domain  | 【4†analytics.pangle-ads.com】\nL39: Duration  | 13 months from the last date it was used  | 13 months from the last date it was used  | 13 months from the last date it was used  | 13 months from the last date it was used  | 13 months from the last date it was used\nL40: Type  | 1st party  | 3rd party  | 1st party  | 1st party  | 3rd party\nL41: Function  | Advertising cookies  | Advertising cookies  | Advertising cookies  | Advertising cookies  | Advertising cookies\nL42: Description  | To measure and improve the performance of advertising campaigns and to personalize the customer experience (including ads) on TikTok.  | To measure and improve the performance of advertising campaigns and to personalize the experience (including ads) on TikTok.  | To measure and improve the performance of advertising campaigns and to personalize the customer experience (including ads) on TikTok.\nL43:  | To measure and improve the performance of advertising campaigns and to personalize the customer experience (including ads) on TikTok.  | To measure and improve the performance of your advertising campaigns and to personalize the customer's ad experiences delivered by the TikTok Pangle ad network.\nL44: ## Next steps\nL45: \nL46:   * Learn 【5†how to use cookies with TikTok Pixel】.\nL47: \nL48: 【6†Image†sf16-website-login.neutral.ttwstatic.com】\nL49: \nL50: Log in for a personalised experience\nL51: \nL52: 【7†Sign up】\nL53: \nL54: Resources\nL55: \nL56: * 【8†TikTok Shop Academy†seller-us.tiktok.com】\nL57: * 【9†TikTok Help Center†support.tiktok.com】\nL58: * 【10†TikTok Academy†www.tiktokacademy.com】\nL59: * 【11†TikTok for Business】\nL60: * 【12†Creative Center】\nL61: * 【13†Agentic Hub】\nL62: \nL63: * 【14†Terms and Policies】\nL64: * 【15†Privacy†www.tiktok.com】\nL65: \nL66: ©2026 TikTok For Business\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBusiness Resource Centre (https://ads.tiktok.com/resources/help/article/how-to-set-up-matching-events-with-events-api)\nciteturn564view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ads.tiktok.com/resources/help/article/how-to-set-up-matching-events-with-events-api\",\"lineno\":3}); Total lines: 36\nL0: 【0†Business Resource Centre】\nL1: \nL2: 【0†Business Help Centre】 【1†Partner enablement】 【2†What's new】\nL3: # How to set up matching events with Events API\nL4: \nL5: Last updated: February 2025\nL6: \nL7: Matching events increase match rates for improved measurement and audience creation.\nL8: \nL9: Send the following keys to measure the impact of your campaigns and attribute actions that take place on your website to ads on TikTok:\nL10:   * Click ID: A unique identifier appended to the URL every time a person clicks on a TikTok ad. Click IDs adhere to the same CTA window configured in your Attribution Manager settings. Learn more about 【3†developer information on implementing Click ID】.\nL11: \nL12:   * Email and Phone (Hashing required): Advanced Matching enables businesses to send hased email and phone to better match website and app Events with ads on TikTok. Learn more about 【4†advanced matching】.\nL13:   * External ID (Hashing required): Advertiser-side identifiers, such as loyalty membership IDs, advertiser customer IDs, and external cookie IDs. Learn more about 【5†external ids】.\nL14: \nL15:   * IP Address (IP) and User Agent (UA): End-user device and connectivity information. IP Address and User Agent are shared by default for Pixel and require manual configuration for Events API. Learn more about 【6†details on IP address and User Agent enablement for Events API†business-api.tiktok.com】.\nL16:   * 1st Party Cookie (if using with Pixel): Unique identifiers saved in the ttp first-party cookie and limited to the advertiser's domain. Learn more about 【6†how to share first-party cookie value with Events API†business-api.tiktok.com】.\nL17: \nL18: 【7†Image†sf16-website-login.neutral.ttwstatic.com】\nL19: \nL20: Log in for a personalised experience\nL21: \nL22: 【8†Sign up】\nL23: \nL24: Resources\nL25: * 【9†TikTok Shop Academy†seller-us.tiktok.com】\nL26: * 【10†TikTok Help Center†support.tiktok.com】\nL27: * 【11†TikTok Academy†www.tiktokacademy.com】\nL28: * 【12†TikTok for Business】\nL29: * 【13†Creative Center】\nL30: * 【14†Agentic Hub】\nL31: \nL32: * 【15†Terms and Policies】\nL33: * 【16†Privacy†www.tiktok.com】\nL34: \nL35: ©2026 TikTok For Business\n"
